# Node
node_modules/

# UE build artifacts — regenerable from source (UBT rebuilds them); untracked
# 2026-06-10 so they stop polluting every diff. Plugins/ is a host-local aura-plugin clone.
UE-projects/CraftBenchTemplate/Intermediate/
UE-projects/CraftBenchTemplate/Saved/
UE-projects/CraftBenchTemplate/Binaries/
UE-projects/CraftBenchTemplate/DerivedDataCache/

# Per-developer AI-tool / editor MCP client configs — not repo artifacts.
# Match anywhere (root and inside the substrate) so they stop polluting git status.
.codex/
.cursor/
.gemini/

# Stray reference PDFs dropped at the repo root. Keep papers under docs/references/
# (tracked deliberately) if the team wants to retain them — not loose at root.
/*.pdf

# Host-local aura-plugin clone (Aura + Ramen). Never committed; created by the
# manual clone-into-Plugins setup step (see docs/WINDOWS.md §3).
/UE-projects/CraftBenchTemplate/Plugins/

# Ephemeral git worktrees the Workflow tool creates for isolated agents.
# Never commit these: each is an embedded git repo, and they are disposable
# (auto-removed when the agent leaves them unchanged).
.claude/worktrees/
runs/.kill-audit.log

# --- generated substrate scratch (2026-08-12) ---------------------------------
# These are TOOL OUTPUT, not source, and leaving them untracked was not free:
# `cb refgate` caches a per-machine certificate that is only valid while the
# task/substrate git tree is clean, so ANY untracked file under a substrate
# invalidates every certificate permanently — each gate then re-grades from
# scratch (~3 min each; three gates on 2026-08-12 cost 600s and cached nothing,
# reporting "PASS not certified — uncommitted changes under the task/substrate").
#
# `.Aura/` is the Aura client's headless-instance state. `_runreport/` is
# the report/preview lane's scratch map directory
# (`CB_GALLERY_MAP` defaults to /Game/Tasks/_runreport/L_Gallery), plus their
# One-File-Per-Actor mirrors, which is where the bulk of the files live.
# Named explicitly rather than globbed: a `_*` pattern under Content/Tasks/
# would silently swallow a future real task id.
UE-projects/*/.Aura/
UE-projects/*/Content/Tasks/_runreport/
UE-projects/*/Content/__ExternalActors__/Tasks/_runreport/
UE-projects/*/Content/__ExternalObjects__/Tasks/_runreport/

# Authoring-lane scratch under a task folder. `.staged/` is the stage-and-grade
# working area and `.baseline-stash/` holds pre-edit copies; both are inputs to
# an authoring script, never deliverables. Ignored because a careless
# `git add -A tasks/` sweeps them in — which is exactly how 21 files of the
# a RETIRED task set got resurrected during the 2026-08-12 rebase
# (caught post-merge; the set had been retired into the baskets upstream).
tasks/*/*/authoring/.staged/
tasks/*/*/authoring/.baseline-stash/

# Rig build-state marker (engine|substrate stamp, stack.py ensure-built lane).
# Machine-local state: must never dirty the substrate tree — an untracked
# marker here made every refgate PASS uncertifiable (2026-08-16 night sweep).
UE-projects/*/.cb-built

# The paper lives in its own repository, and is sometimes cloned here for
# convenience. A nested checkout must never be added to THIS one: `git add`
# would record it as a gitlink to a commit no clone of craftbench can resolve,
# and CI's inventory check reads `git ls-files`.
/paper/

# Working spreadsheets (task slates, eval sheets, prompt corpora). They are
# review material, not repo artefacts, and a binary .xlsx cannot be reviewed in
# a diff.
*.xlsx

# The proxy's marker census (`CB_PROXY_MARKER_CENSUS`, aura_rig/proxy.py) — a
# RUNTIME log that lands wherever the proxy was started from, not source. One
# copy reached a commit; the pattern is unanchored so it cannot again from a
# different cwd.
marker_census.jsonl

# --- Epic Games template content — REGENERATED, never committed (2026-08-30) --
# CraftBench cannot relicense material it does not own, and the UE EULA
# restricts redistributing engine Content to Engine Licensees — which a public
# repo cannot guarantee its readers are. So the 881 Epic-authored Content files
# (260 MB) were removed and are restored from the reader's own UE 5.8 install by
# the bootstrap step in the README. These rules keep a regenerated copy from
# being accidentally committed back.
#
# Each rule names an exact Epic subdirectory. Do NOT collapse the
# __External*__ rules into a bare `__ExternalActors__/`: those One-File-Per-
# Actor trees are SPLIT. 479 actor + 42 object sidecars mirror the Epic maps
# below and are regenerated; the other 286 + 9 sit under `Maps/` and are OURS —
# the committed task maps, which are the benchmark itself. A rule broad enough
# to swallow `__ExternalActors__/Maps/` would silently untrack task content and
# turn an L2 grade into a FAIL.
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/Characters/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/ThirdPerson/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/Variant_Combat/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/Variant_SideScrolling/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/Variant_Platforming/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/LevelPrototyping/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/Input/
UE-projects/CraftBenchTemplate/Content/Characters/

# OFPA sidecars for the Epic maps only — `Maps/` is deliberately absent.
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalActors__/ThirdPerson/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalActors__/Variant_Combat/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalActors__/Variant_SideScrolling/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalActors__/Variant_Platforming/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalObjects__/ThirdPerson/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalObjects__/Variant_Combat/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalObjects__/Variant_SideScrolling/
UE-projects/ThirdPerson/Content/__ExternalObjects__/Variant_Platforming/
